                <pb facs="0572" n="566" sameAs="frus:frus1894app1/pg566"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Foster to Mr. Herbert.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-09-27"><hi rendition="#italic">September 27,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to send you a copy of a
                    note under date of August 13 which I have received from the German chargé in
                    this city, relative to a proposed fee of $5, which it is understood the chief
                    justice of Samoa intends to impose for the registration of every separate title
                    to land. I also inclose a copy of my reply, and should be glad to be informed of
                    the opinion of Her Majesty’s Government upon this subject.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John W. Foster.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
